ne article adds that extreme poverty fell from 6.2% to 5.7%, and general monetary poverty dropped from 29% to 27.6%, ending three consecutive years of increases.\n- **Source data:** The data comes from the Encuesta Nacional de Hogares (ENAHO), which INEI has conducted for more than 20 years.\n- **Earlier age-band reference (2021):** INEI reported that 35.4% of the population aged 0 to 17 was in poverty. This is older and not 2024 data.\n\nTo get the 0–14 rate, check the INEI \"Evolución de la Pobreza Monetaria 2015–2024\" technical report or its annual poverty tables on inei.gob.pe, which break incidence down by age group. I did not open those documents, so I can't confirm a 0–14 figure from them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "16275269-e0e2-4618-8d3d-d3335da26099", "uuid": "0d0aca1c-8c56-45e8-8c06-7ebc3c5dc41f", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T22:09:39.666Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "INEI pobreza monetaria 2024 población de 0 a 14 años porcentaje ENAHO", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01R3MUZaawy32bSf6xZyWaBR", "content": [{"title": "24122025%20INFORME%20DE%20PROGRESO%20EN%20LOS%20OBJETIVOS%20DE%20DESARROLLO%20SOSTENIBLE compressed.pdf", "url": "https://www.unicef.org/peru/media/20366/file/24122025%20INFORME%20DE%20PROGRESO%20EN%20LOS%20OBJETIVOS%20DE%20DESARROLLO%20SOSTENIBLE_compressed.pdf.pdf"}, {"title": "www.unicef.org", "url": "https://www.unicef.org/peru/media/9026/file/Reporte%20técnico.pdf"}, {"title": "5 Boletin Mayo 146", "url": "https://bcasas.org.pe/wp-content/uploads/5_Boletin_Mayo-146.pdf"}, {"title": "www.inei.gob.pe", "url": "https://www.inei.gob.pe/media/MenuRecursivo/publicaciones_digitales/Est/Lib1047/Libro.pdf"}, {"title": "lacamara.pe", "url": "https://lacamara.pe/tag/rural/?print=pdf"}, {"title": "1ppt. cesip. cr. jue10jul", "url": "https://www.congreso.gob.pe/Docs/comisiones2021/CESIP-OCDE/files/1ppt._cesip._cr._jue